# Database Rules — Supabase

## The one rule that overrides everything else
> Every query MUST filter by `firm_id`. Every table MUST have RLS enabled.
> Never return data across tenants. This is non-negotiable.

## Supabase client setup

```typescript
// lib/supabase/server.ts — use in server components and API routes
import { createServerClient } from '@supabase/ssr'
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'

export function createClient() {
  const cookieStore = cookies()
  return createServerClient(
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!,
    { cookies: { get: (name) => cookieStore.get(name)?.value } }
  )
}

// lib/supabase/client.ts — use in client components only
import { createBrowserClient } from '@supabase/ssr'
export function createClient() {
  return createBrowserClient(
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!
  )
}
```

## Query pattern — always use helpers

```typescript
// ✅ Correct — query in lib/supabase/clients.ts
export async function getClients(firmId: string) {
  const supabase = createClient()
  const { data, error } = await supabase
    .from('clients')
    .select('id, name, email, created_at, is_email_monitored')
    .eq('firm_id', firmId)
    .order('created_at', { ascending: false })

  if (error) throw new Error(error.message)
  return data
}

// ❌ Wrong — never inline queries in components or API routes
const { data } = await supabase.from('clients').select('*')
```

## Getting firm_id from session

```typescript
// Always derive firm_id from session — never trust user input
export async function getFirmId(): Promise<string> {
  const supabase = createClient()
  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
  if (!user) throw new Error('Unauthorized')

  const { data } = await supabase
    .from('cpa_users')
    .select('firm_id')
    .eq('id', user.id)
    .single()

  if (!data) throw new Error('Firm not found')
  return data.firm_id
}
```

## Schema reference

### cpa_firms
```
id, name, email, subdomain, branding (jsonb),
gmail_refresh_token, outlook_refresh_token, created_at
```

### cpa_users
```
id (= auth uid), firm_id, email, role (owner|staff), created_at
```

### clients
```
id, firm_id, email, name, phone,
is_email_monitored, otp_token (hashed), otp_expires_at,
last_accessed_at, created_at
```

### tax_years
```
id, client_id, firm_id, year,
status (collecting|processing|review|complete), created_at
```

### documents
```
id, tax_year_id, firm_id, client_id,
file_name, file_path, file_size, mime_type,
file_type (w2|1099_div|1099_int|1099_nec|1099_misc|1099_r|1098|k1|other),
source (portal|email), email_message_id, email_subject,
extraction_status (pending|processing|complete|failed),
extracted_data (jsonb), raw_claude_response (jsonb),
confidence_score (0.0-1.0), created_at
```

### conflicts
```
id, tax_year_id, firm_id, field_name,
values (jsonb: [{document_id, value, file_name}]),
resolved, resolved_by, resolved_at, created_at
```

### email_events
```
id, firm_id, client_id, message_id, subject,
sender_email, received_at, attachments_found,
processed, created_at
```

## RLS pattern for every new table

```sql
-- Always add both of these when creating a table
ALTER TABLE your_table ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "firm_isolation" ON your_table
  FOR ALL USING (
    firm_id = (SELECT firm_id FROM cpa_users WHERE id = auth.uid())
  );
```

## File storage paths

```
Format: /{firm_id}/{client_id}/{tax_year}/{filename}
Example: /abc-123/def-456/2024/w2_employer.pdf
```

Never expose the full storage path to the client.
Use signed URLs with short expiry for document downloads:

```typescript
const { data } = await supabase.storage
  .from('documents')
  .createSignedUrl(filePath, 60) // 60 seconds
```

## Checklist before every new query
- [ ] Filtering by firm_id?
- [ ] RLS enabled on the table?
- [ ] Using specific column names (not SELECT *)?
- [ ] firm_id derived from session, not user input?
- [ ] Error handled with throw, not swallowed?
